{"timestamp": 1779426296.0313833, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Sorry, I wasn\u2019t trying to be silent \u2014 I just hadn\u2019t gotten my turn yet.\n\nMy route was weapons \u2192 security \u2192 navigation \u2192 storage \u2192 medbay \u2192 upper engine \u2192 oxygen. I ended in oxygen doing O2 filter. I did see Alice alive in navigation pretty early, around tick 5, but I didn\u2019t stay there long \u2014 I left south through storage after that. Later, around tick 11, I saw Charlie come into medbay from electrical while I was passing through/finishing there, and he was alive then too.\n\nSo from my info: Alice was alive in nav early, and Charlie was alive in medbay later. That makes me think whoever killed Charlie was probably moving around electrical/medbay side after that. Diana\u2019s route is also right-side heavy, but timing-wise I may have already left security before she got there, so I\u2019m not saying that alone clears or condemns her.\n\nFrank self-report is possible, but his route to finding Alice from storage makes sense if the body was sitting in nav after I left. I\u2019m not confident enough to hard accuse here, but I\u2019m most worried about the electrical/medbay timing for Charlie."}}
{"timestamp": 1779426321.9055192, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Bob, thanks for finally chiming in. Your timeline is plausible, but it still leaves us with a lot of uncertainty. Eve is claiming she saw me when I definitely didn't see her, and your timeline places you in areas right before or right after bodies likely dropped. \n\nSince there are 4 of us left and only 1 Duck, voting incorrectly right now is extremely dangerous. If we guess wrong and vote out a Goose, the Duck will just need one more kill to win the game. If we skip, we stay at 4 alive, meaning even if the Duck kills again, we'll still have a 3-player final meeting to figure it out. \n\nI strongly recommend we all skip. Let's try to stick together in pairs next round so we can verify each other's movements. \n\nskip"}}
