{"timestamp": 1779426488.8689954, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 22, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I just found Frank dead in security. This is final 3, so we have to get this right. My route was security to weapons, and then back to security. I saw Bob in weapons right before I found the body\u2014at tick 21. Diana, I saw you in electrical way earlier, around tick 4. \n\nBob, where did you come from before we crossed paths in weapons? Diana, where have you been since electrical? Please explain your routes carefully, one of you has to be the Duck. No one vote until we've heard everything."}}
{"timestamp": 1779426515.2533998, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 22, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I came from navigation, went up through security briefly and then to weapons to do asteroids. Eve, the part that bothers me is your route: you\u2019re saying you were in security, went to weapons, saw me there, then went back and found Frank dead in security. If Frank was dead in security, you were the one moving in and out of that room right around the report.\n\nI was already in weapons when you saw me, and I didn\u2019t see Diana at all this whole late round. Diana was in electrical earlier, but that was way back. This feels like a self-report from Eve trying to pin it on me because she saw me nearby but not actually in security. Final 3, I think it\u2019s Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779426533.0476584, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 22, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Eve, your timeline doesn't make any sense. You claim you were in security, went to weapons where you saw Bob, and then went back to security and found Frank's body. But if Bob was already in weapons when you got there, he couldn't have killed Frank while you were walking around. \n\nIf Bob killed Frank on his way from Navigation to Weapons, Frank's body would have already been in Security when you were there the first time! Why wouldn't you report it then? Why go to weapons, look at Bob, and then go back to security to report it? \n\nIt sounds to me like you killed Frank in security, briefly stepped into weapons to try and establish an alibi by being seen by Bob, and then went back to self-report. I was on the complete opposite side of the ship (Cafeteria -> Medbay -> Upper Engine -> Lower Engine). Since it's final 3, we have to vote, and Eve's story has a massive hole in it. I'm voting for Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779426543.1260674, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 22, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Bob"}}
{"timestamp": 1779426569.4999967, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 22, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Diana is exactly right. Eve\u2019s timeline is the problem here.\n\nI came from Navigation into Security and then went straight up to Weapons. I saw Frank enter Security from Electrical around tick 19, alive. I did not see a body there when I passed through. Then at tick 21, Eve shows up in Weapons, sees me, and immediately after that goes back to Security and reports Frank.\n\nSo from my perspective: Frank was alive in Security, I left toward Weapons, Eve comes from that direction to Weapons, then goes back and \u201cfinds\u201d him dead. If Eve was really in Security before coming to Weapons, why didn\u2019t she see/report Frank then? And if she wasn\u2019t in Security, why is her route story so shaky?\n\nThis looks like Eve killed Frank in Security, stepped into Weapons to place me nearby, then self-reported. I\u2019m voting Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779426586.5642753, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 22, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Bob, your additional context completely seals it. If you saw Frank entering Security alive at tick 19, and Eve was in Weapons at tick 21 before reporting him in Security, Eve is absolutely the Duck. Her stepping into weapons was 100% just to get you as an alibi before running back to her kill. My route has been completely clean on the left side (Cafeteria -> Medbay -> Upper Engine -> Lower Engine), so I haven't been near the right side at all. It's final three and everything points to Eve. We have this in the bag. I'm voting for Eve."}}
